"toolCallId":"toolu_01K41N8FQnAC2Ei9ogzF6hen","toolName":"xorq_catalog_schema","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Type: Source (bound)\n\nSchema Out:\n  SUMLEV                   int64\n  REGION                   string\n  DIVISION                 string\n  STATE                    int64\n  NAME                     string\n  ESTIMATESBASE2020        int64\n  POPESTIMATE2020          int64\n  POPESTIMATE2021          int64\n  POPESTIMATE2022          int64\n  POPESTIMATE2023          int64\n  POPESTIMATE2024          int64\n  POPESTIMATE2025          int64\n  NPOPCHG_2020             int64\n  NPOPCHG_2021             int64\n  NPOPCHG_2022             int64\n  NPOPCHG_2023             int64\n  NPOPCHG_2024             int64\n  NPOPCHG_2025             int64\n  BIRTHS2020               int64\n  BIRTHS2021               int64\n  BIRTHS2022               int64\n  BIRTHS2023               int64\n  BIRTHS2024               int64\n  BIRTHS2025               int64\n  DEATHS2020               int64\n  DEATHS2021               int64\n  DEATHS2022               int64\n  DEATHS2023               int64\n  DEATHS2024               int64\n  DEATHS2025               int64\n  NATURALCHG2020           int64\n  NATURALCHG2021           int64\n  NATURALCHG2022           int64\n  NATURALCHG2023           int64\n  NATURALCHG2024           int64\n  NATURALCHG2025           int64\n  INTERNATIONALMIG2020     int64\n  INTERNATIONALMIG2021     int64\n  INTERNATIONALMIG2022     int64\n  INTERNATIONALMIG2023     int64\n  INTERNATIONALMIG2024     int64\n  INTERNATIONALMIG2025     int64\n  DOMESTICMIG2020          int64\n  DOMESTICMIG2021          int64\n  DOMESTICMIG2022          int64\n  DOMESTICMIG2023          int64\n  DOMESTICMIG2024          int64\n  DOMESTICMIG2025          int64\n  NETMIG2020               int64\n  NETMIG2021               int64\n  NETMIG2022               int64\n  NETMIG2023               int64\n  NETMIG2024               int64\n  NETMIG2025               int64\n  RESIDUAL2020             int64\n  RESIDUAL2021             int64\n  RESIDUAL2022             int64\n  RESIDUAL2023             int64\n  RESIDUAL2024             int64\n  RESIDUAL2025             int64\n  GQESTIMATESBASE2020      int64\n  GQESTIMATES2020          int64\n  GQESTIMATES2021          int64\n  GQESTIMATES2022          int64\n  GQESTIMATES2023          int64\n  GQESTIMATES2024          int64\n  GQESTIMATES2025          int64\n  RBIRTH2021               float64\n  RBIRTH2022               float64\n  RBIRTH2023               float64\n  RBIRTH2024               float64\n  RBIRTH2025               float64\n  RDEATH2021               float64\n  RDEATH2022               float64\n  RDEATH2023               float64\n  RDEATH2024               float64\n  RDEATH2025               float64\n  RNATURALCHG2021          float64\n  RNATURALCHG2022          float64\n  RNATURALCHG2023          float64\n  RNATURALCHG2024          float64\n  RNATURALCHG2025          float64\n  RINTERNATIONALMIG2021    float64\n  RINTERNATIONALMIG2022    float64\n  RINTERNATIONALMIG2023    float64\n  RINTERNATIONALMIG2024    float64\n  RINTERNATIONALMIG2025    float64\n  RDOMESTICMIG2021         float64\n  RDOMESTICMIG2022         float64\n  RDOMESTICMIG2023         float64\n  RDOMESTICMIG2024         float64\n  RDOMESTICMIG2025         float64\n  RNETMIG2021              float64\n  RNETMIG2022              float64\n  RNETMIG2023              float64\n  RNETMIG2024              float64\n  RNETMIG2025              float64\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786915447329},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Perfect! Now I understand the structure:\n\n1. farmers-markets has:\n   - state_name\n   - farmers_markets (column with the count)\n\n2. census has:\n   - NAME (state name)\n   - POPESTIMATE2025 (2025 population estimate)\n   - SUMLEV (summary level - I need to filter for the US total, which is SUMLEV=10)\n\nNow I need to create a script that:\n1. Gets the total farmers markets (sum of the farmers_markets column)\n2. Gets the US population (POPESTIMATE2025 where SUMLEV=10 or the US total)\n3. Calculates farmers_markets_per_100k = (total_farmers_markets / total_population) * 100000\n\nLet me create a cross-dataset build script that joins these together.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Now I'll create a derived metric that calculates farmers markets per 100,000 residents:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01GEYz4V6BdEPHQpaXXV9Tcy","name":"write","arguments":{"path":".xorq/scripts/build_markets_per_capita.py","content":"import urllib.request as u\n_o = u.build_opener(); _o.addheaders = [(\"User-Agent\", \"Mozilla/5.0\")]; u.install_opener(_o)\n\nfrom xorq.vendor.ibis.common.collections import FrozenDict\nimport xorq.api as xo\nso = FrozenDict({\"User-Agent\": \"Mozilla/5.0\"})\ncon = xo.pandas.connect()\n\n# Read farmers markets data and sum the total\nmarkets = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"markets\", storage_options=so)\ntotal_markets = markets.aggregate(total_farmers_markets=markets.farmers_markets.sum())\n\n# Read census data and get US total population (SUMLEV=10 is US)\ncensus = xo.deferred_read_csv(\n    \"https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv\",\n    con, table_name=\"census\", storage_options=so)\nus_pop = (census.filter(census.SUMLEV == 10)\n          .select(\"POPESTIMATE2025\").mutate(k=xo.literal(1)))\n\n# Join on constant key and calculate the metric\nexpr = (\n    total_markets.mutate(k=xo.literal(1))\n      .join(us_pop, total_markets.k == us_pop.k)\n      .mutate(markets_per_100k=(total_markets.total_farmers_markets / us_pop.POPESTIMATE2025) * 100000)\n      .select(\"total_farmers_markets\", \"POPESTIMATE2025\", \"markets_per_100k\")\n)\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":14,"outpu